            tagline = "A floating library changes its route after listening to its readers.",
            parts = listOf(
                StoryPart(1, "A Boat of Books", listOf("Every Wednesday, a small library boat visited communities along the river. When the librarian became ill, Ada volunteered to help organise shelves under the coordinator's supervision.", "She noticed that one village had stopped borrowing books altogether, although the boat's route log said it still visited.", "The coordinator, Mr Bello, suggested they learn what had changed before assuming readers had lost interest.")),
                StoryPart(2, "The Empty Register", listOf("The borrowing register showed that the village once had many readers. Then entries stopped, even though the route log showed visits.", "Ada compared dates with weather notices and found several cancelled trips that had not been recorded accurately.", "The crew agreed to ask residents about the best landing point and improve the records.")),
                StoryPart(3, "A Message in a Book", listOf("A returned storybook contained a bookmark: 'Please bring books that explain the stars.' No name was attached.", "Ada placed the request on the boat's noticeboard and asked the village teacher whether an astronomy club had started.", "The teacher said students had been studying the night sky, but their classroom library had few science books.")),
                StoryPart(4, "The New Landing", listOf("The village head showed Ada and Mr Bello a safer public landing farther upstream. The old landing had become difficult to reach when water levels changed.", "The coordinator checked the route with local authorities and confirmed where the boat could stop without blocking river traffic.", "Residents suggested a supervised book collection point at the school for days when the boat could not visit.")),
                StoryPart(5, "Books for the Sky", listOf("Ada prepared a list of age-appropriate astronomy books and observation guides. The teacher reviewed the titles and requested books about local weather and moon phases.", "A science volunteer offered to lead a reading session and explain how to record observations carefully.", "The bookmark's writer turned out to be a student named Lami, who was delighted when the new books arrived.")),
                StoryPart(6, "The Lost Box", listOf("During inventory, Ada discovered a box of donated books missing from the boat's records. The last entry said it had been unloaded at the old landing.", "The crew checked the storage room and asked the school whether the box had been delivered there by mistake.", "A teacher found it in a locked storeroom, still labelled for the library boat. The delivery had been moved during the route change.")),
                StoryPart(7, "A Better Register", listOf("Ada and the coordinator created a simpler register showing books loaded, delivered, returned, and temporarily stored. Each village received a copy of its delivery record.", "They added a section for cancelled visits and a way to request books without displaying personal details publicly.", "The new process made it easier to find missing boxes and plan the next trip.")),
                StoryPart(8, "The Reading Festival", listOf("The school hosted a riverside reading festival. Children read stories aloud, older students displayed science notebooks, and adults exchanged books.", "Lami presented a star chart she had made over several weeks. She explained which observations were hers and which facts came from books.", "Ada recorded the event's requests and promised to bring the list to the coordinator.")),
                StoryPart(9, "A Route That Listens", listOf("The library boat returned with requested titles and a revised schedule. The crew consulted residents about landing conditions and announced changes through the school and noticeboard.", "The village's borrowing register began filling again. Some readers borrowed novels, others requested exam guides, and families used the collection point when they could not meet the boat.", "Ada realised the route was not just a line on water. It was an agreement that had to adapt to the people it served.")),
                StoryPart(10, "The Next Crossing", listOf("At the end of term, the coordinator thanked Ada for improving the records and helping the village rebuild its reading habit.", "The boat's next route included a stop for another community that had requested children's books. Ada returned the bookmark to Lami, who tucked it into a new astronomy book.", "As the boat moved along the river, Ada understood that a library was not only a building. Sometimes it was a promise that knowledge would keep finding its way to people."))
